docs(go-live): add v1.1 PSK + tenant + GHCR pre-flight checks

Roadmap item 19. Extends scripts/nexora-go-live-check.sh with the
v1.1 secrets/state surface so the operator can't flip DNS with a
half-configured updater path.

New checks:
  - NEXORA_UPDATER_PSK length on backend (≥32 chars, openssl rand
    -hex 32 hint surfaced on fail).
  - NEXORA_UPDATER_PSK on the updater container too, and that the
    two lengths match — a length mismatch guarantees handshake
    failure, surface as FAIL not WARN.
  - updater container running check (warn-only — auto-update is
    optional; manual docker compose still works without it).
  - /data/app/license.lic presence (warn — encrypted snapshots
    fall back to plain tar.gz without it).
  - /data/app/machine-id presence + size (warn — ensureMachineId()
    will mint on next boot but pre-existing snapshots break).
  - GHCR_TOKEN / NEXORA_GHCR_TOKEN length (warn — only required
    for private per-customer image customers).

Severity choices:
  - PSK mismatch is FAIL: handshakes break silently if lengths drift.
  - Everything else WARN: degraded but operational paths.

Syntax: bash -n passes.
No prod code touched — pure script + docs surface.